content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-108 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23110, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.2 mm/s against Figure 3 of the HF-300 manual. It is in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'). It is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A boundary and below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C 'Restricted – plan maintenance' and 7.1 mm/s Zone D 'stop the pump' thresholds. No stop is required on vibration. The report does not state whether the value is RMS, or whether it is the highest reading from both bearing housings as the manual requires.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature 68 C against the manual specification. It is within the normal range (normal up to 70 C; alarm 80 C; trip 90 C), with only 2 C margin to the top of normal. Temperatures are measured on the housing surface, which matches the reported drive-end housing reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft seal leakage of about one drop every two seconds. The troubleshooting table lists 'Leakage at shaft seal' as a symptom requiring mechanical seal replacement (5.2) and an alignment check (5.4). The evidence gives no numeric acceptable leakage rate, so the drip cannot be compared to a limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Early failure of the original-style component seal HF3-450. Service bulletin SB-2026-014 reports field failures of HF3-450 on pumps from serial HF3-22000 onward, caused by a revised sleeve tolerance. P-108 (HF3-23110) is in this range.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal has run dry, for example through loss of Plan 11 flush from the pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is also a listed cause of vibration and bearing temperature, both of which are within limits but not in the lowest band.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Confirm P-108 serial HF3-23110 on the nameplate. Confirm that cartridge seal HF3-450B (not HF3-450), shaft sleeve HF3-455 (contingency) and casing gasket HF3-120 are on hand before starting.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, record vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Record drive-end and non-drive-end housing temperatures as the baseline.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and sleeve. Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring and replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, check the drive-end (6312-C3) and non-drive-end (6310-C3) bearings for wear or noise. If either is worn, replace both as a pair per 5.3. This is a separate 6.0 h, 2-technician job and should be raised as a new request.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new cartridge seal HF3-450B. It is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Torque the seal gland nuts (M10) to 30 Nm per SB-2026-014. This replaces the 25 Nm in manual Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Refit the impeller and torque the impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm, lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Refit the back pull-out assembly and torque the casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm, lightly oiled threads. Torque the bearing housing bolts (M12) to 85 Nm if they were disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align pump and motor, because back pull-out removal disturbs the bearing housing and misalignment is a listed seal-leak cause. Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm, angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from the pump discharge is in place and the pump is fully filled before start. Never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, check the seal for leakage. Re-measure vibration on both housings against Figure 3 (target Zone A/B, below 4.5 mm/s) and housing temperature against the 70 C normal limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set. Supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, to be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, contingency. Fit only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before any dismantling.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not start the pump dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush and that the casing is filled before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not fit seal HF3-450 on this pump (serial HF3-23110). Fitting it repeats the known early-failure mode.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency only, if bearings are found worn: bearing pair replacement, 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number conflict. Manual parts list item 3 gives component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) says do not fit HF3-450 on HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. P-108 serial HF3-23110 is above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies and HF3-450B must be used.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque conflict. Manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, but SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because P-108 is in the bulletin's serial range and will receive HF3-450B, 30 Nm applies. Table 5 (25 Nm with HF3-450) applies only to pumps below HF3-22000.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve handling difference. Manual 5.2 says to inspect the sleeve for scoring with no acceptance figure. The bulletin states HF3-450B needs no sleeve measurement but sets a 0.1 mm scoring depth replacement limit for HF3-455. The bulletin's limit applies to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bulletin changes only the gland torque. Manual Table 5 values for casing bolts (210 Nm), impeller nut (160 Nm) and bearing housing bolts (85 Nm) are not contradicted and are used as written.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "No acceptable shaft seal leakage rate is documented, so the one drop every two seconds cannot be compared with a limit or used to set urgency precisely.",
    "It is unconfirmed whether the 3.2 mm/s vibration is RMS and is the highest reading across both bearing housings, as Figure 3 and section 3 require.",
    "Non-drive-end bearing housing temperature and the temperature trend are not reported. The drive end at 68 C is close to the 70 C normal limit.",
    "It is unknown whether P-108 currently has HF3-450 or HF3-450B fitted, which affects whether the bulletin failure mode is the likely cause.",
    "The date of the fault report and the last seal change are not given relative to the bulletin issue date (14 March 2026). Applicability here is decided by serial number.",
    "The evidence gives no grease type or quantity, impeller nut reuse or replacement guidance, or lockout and permit specifics beyond 'isolate and drain'.",
    "No NPSH or suction data is available to rule out cavitation as a contributor to vibration or seal distress."
  ]
}
